{
  "_about": "Component spec for pos-multiselect (docs/inspect refactor, component migration batch, 2026-08-26). Single source of truth for the Variants/Usage/Tokens tabs on /style-guide \"Multiselect\" section. Reuses the already-curated usage prose from COMP_CONFIGS['multiselect'].usage and token data from COMP_CONFIGS['multiselect'].tokens (verified-accurate, currently-live data) restructured into the new schema. Single representative variant — this component's preview shows one instance (no Variant/Base toggle needed per the 2026-08-25/26 \"multiple sub-variants side by side\" rule). Regenerate the spec partial with the script in RULES.md 6.4 if the source data changes; do not hand-edit token values here. Updated 2026-08-27: the opened-state Color list had --pos-color-page-background left over from before the .pos-form-multiselect-selected-item CSS fix (was page-background, is now highlight-background) — corrected to --pos-color-highlight-background to match. Updated 2026-08-27: added usageExample/props/composedOf (Target architecture point 1 fields that were left empty when this spec was first generated).",
  "component": "multiselect",
  "name": "Multiselect",
  "description": "Letting users select multiple values from a defined list — tags, categories, filters, permissions.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Letting users select multiple values from a defined list — tags, categories, filters, permissions.",
    "The set of choices is too long for a group of checkboxes (more than 5–7 options).",
    "Selected items should be visible inline without opening a panel."
  ],
  "whenNotToUse": [
    "Only one item can ever be selected — use a <code>select</code> element instead.",
    "The list has fewer than 5 options — inline checkboxes are more accessible."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Always associate a visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> with the multiselect via <code>id</code>.",
    "Pre-select the most common choices when a sensible default exists.",
    "Use <code>multiline</code> when several items are likely to be selected at once and the layout has vertical room to spare — instead of growing wider, the field keeps its default width and wraps the selected tags onto extra lines.",
    "Use <code>combined</code> when the list is long and the field must stay a predictable, compact width regardless of how many items get selected — it replaces the individual tags with a single \"N selected\" summary once 2 or more are chosen.",
    "Use <code>showFilter</code> when the option list is long enough that scanning it is slower than typing a few letters to narrow it down (roughly 10+ options)."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "Use multiselect for binary or single-choice selection — use checkboxes or a select instead.",
    "Leave the placeholder blank — always describe what kind of options are inside.",
    "Combine <code>multiline</code> and <code>combined</code> on the same instance — they solve the same \"too many tags\" problem in opposite ways (wrap vs. summarize), so only one should be enabled at a time.",
    "Enable <code>showFilter</code> on a short list (under ~10 options) — it adds a step for no benefit."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "Every multiselect must have a programmatically associated <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>.",
    "The input container has <code>tabindex=\"0\"</code> and <code>aria-expanded</code> to announce open/closed state to screen readers.",
    "Each option uses a <code>&lt;checkbox&gt;</code> so screen readers can navigate and toggle individual items.",
    "Disabled: set <code>aria-disabled=\"true\"</code> and <code>tabindex=\"-1\"</code> on <code>.pos-form-multiselect-input</code> — the init click guard and the module's keydown handler both read it, so the field can't be opened or cleared by mouse or keyboard."
  ],
  "composedOf": [
    "tag",
    "checkbox",
    "control-icons"
  ],
  "props": [
    {
      "name": "pos-form-multiselect-multiline",
      "type": "boolean class",
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Field keeps its default width and wraps selected tags onto extra lines instead of growing wider."
    },
    {
      "name": "pos-form-multiselect-combine",
      "type": "boolean class",
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Replaces individual tags with a single \"N selected\" summary once 2+ are chosen — keeps the field a predictable compact width."
    },
    {
      "name": "showFilter",
      "type": "JS module option",
      "default": "false",
      "description": "Adds a text filter above the option list — for long lists (~10+ options)."
    }
  ],
  "dimensions": {
    "state": [
      "closed",
      "hover",
      "focus",
      "opened",
      "filled",
      "disabled"
    ]
  },
